\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab Child sexual abuse material (CSAM);\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab Hosting illegal marketplaces or services;\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab Use by sanctioned individuals or entities;\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab Export or operation outside India (Products);\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab Circumventing lawful court orders;\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab {\b Destroying, altering, or concealing evidence subject to a known legal hold, court order, or active investigation;}\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab {\b Covert surveillance or monitoring of any individual without lawful authority and without any notice or consent required by applicable law \u8212? including any use against a spouse, partner, family member, or other individual as "stalkerware";}\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab {\b Remotely locking, wiping, or otherwise acting on any device that the Customer does not own or lack authority to manage;}\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\sb40\sa40\bullet\tab {\b Infringing intellectual-property rights, including software piracy or circumvention of technological protection measures.}\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 Violation constitutes material breach and may result in termination.\par
\pard\sb200\sa80\b\fs22 14. Warranty & Disclaimers\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sb140\sa60\b 14.1 Limited Hardware Warranty\b0\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 {\b Coverage.} ServaLabs warrants Product hardware against manufacturing defects for {\b twelve (12) months from Delivery} (as defined in Section 2). The sole and exclusive remedy is repair or replacement at ServaLabs' option.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 {\b Who holds the warranty.} In a direct sale the warranty is personal to the Customer. {\b In a Reseller Sale the benefit of the warranty passes with the Product to the first end customer on the reseller's onward sale, for the unexpired remainder of the period} \u8212? no ServaLabs consent is required for that passage, and Section 15.8 does not restrict it. Because the period runs from Delivery to the reseller, the remainder available to the end customer is reduced by the time the reseller held the unit; ServaLabs requires the reseller to disclose the actual expiry date at the point of sale (Section 4.4(d)). Any {\b further} transfer, for example on a subsequent resale of the hardware, requires ServaLabs' consent under Section 15.8.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 {\b Exclusions.} The warranty does not cover damage caused by: misuse, accident, or neglect; operation outside the environmental requirements of Section 6.4 (including water exposure, improper voltage, shock, vibration, or temperature extremes); or modification or repair by the Customer or third parties, to the extent the damage is caused by that modification or repair. Opening the chassis, replacing or adding drives, or installing the Customer's own software does not by itself void this warranty.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 {\b RMA Process & Shipping.} Warranty service requires a return merchandise authorization (RMA) issued by ServaLabs. {\b Where the unit is confirmed to have a defect covered by this warranty, ServaLabs bears the cost of shipping in both directions.} Where the reported fault is not found, or is excluded under this Section, the Customer bears the cost of shipping to ServaLabs. Risk of loss in transit lies with the party arranging and paying for that leg. In a Reseller Sale the Customer may raise a warranty claim with ServaLabs directly or through its reseller.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 {\b Customer Data During Service.} Products use separate boot and data drives. The Customer is strongly advised to remove its data drives before shipping a unit for service \u8212? warranty service does not require them. If the Customer ships a unit with data drives installed, ServaLabs will not access, read, or copy any data on them, and any storage media replaced during service is securely erased or physically destroyed before disposal or reuse. The Customer remains responsible for backing up its data before any service event (Section 17.4).\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 {\b DOA.} A unit that fails on initial installation or within the Inspection Period (Section 7.2) is treated as DOA and prioritized for replacement.\par
\pard\sb140\sa60\b 14.2 Comprehensive Warranty Disclaimer\b0\par
